{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/354583-wrestling-focused-hunter","id":354583,"title":"Wrestling Focused Hunter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-30T02:03:07-08:00","id":354583,"title":"Wrestling Focused Hunter","content":"In an upcoming game we will be playing close approximations of ourselves in a Hunter game. I'm pretty good at wrestling so I took Brawl \u00b0\u00b0 with a grapple specialty &amp; Grapple Style \u00b0\u00b0\u00b0 &amp; Police Tactics \u00b0 for compliance hold. But then I started thinking that trying to grapple a vampire or werewolf is a seriously bad idea &amp; I should instead switch focus. Is being a grappler a good idea or should I spend my points else where? (We are using GMC rules)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T02:05:29-08:00","id":354615,"title":"","content":"If you want to be competent a fight with a monster I would strongly suggest a hunter focused on using weapons, grappling a vampire is a bad idea unless you have a useful Endowment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-30-2014, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T03:17:41-08:00","id":354647,"title":"","content":"The compliance hold is exactly what it sounds like: it's good if you can bring overwhelming force to a situation in order to surround an enemy and take him alive. As a hunter in presumably a small cell with no special resources backing you, you're probably not going to be overwhelming a werewolf enough to be able to safely wrestle it to the ground and cuff it anytime soon. Try mentally substituting a bear and asking the same question; you're gonna want a big gun and a big head start to run, not a German suplex.<br /> <br /> The point of playing a Hunter game statted as approximations of yourselves might not be to actually be well equipped to fight monsters, though, so maybe check with your friends and see how their builds are. If your group is going with having fun panicking and applying niche skills to the Vigil, you could still get mileage out of, say, ganging up and isolating one of the vampire's servants in order to kidnap and interrogate him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 12-30-2014, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T04:21:38-08:00","id":354663,"title":"","content":"This question really has two answers, depending on the assumptions you bring to the table.<br /> <br /> The first assumption is that you want to play yourselves, ie reasonably normal individuals, dragged into fighting the supernatural to protect people. In which case, you should focus on modelling yourselves, and trust the ST to handle encounters in such a way to be fun. You won't be especially effective most likely (my gaming group actually includes a guy who studies Haidong Gumdo and is pretty big, so can actually justify points in Weaponry, but I suspect that's unusual), but in fairness that's what Hunter <i>is</i>, normal people doing their best in a fight they're woefully unsuited and unequipped for, and if your ST handles it right, you can have a lot of fun with that. As Loserman suggests, you'd likely end up working not on killing the vampire themselves 99% of the time, you'd probably work on the more vulnerable aspects, like servants and businesses: a vampire draws its resources partially from an electronics store owned by a ghoul? One molotov cocktail will put a crimp in his wallet pretty soon, and poses little direct threat to you, at least in the short-term. Which, in my view, is way more fun, and I wished I got to play in that kind of game more often. However, if you do end up directly facing a vampire or werewolf pack, you're probably pretty screwed.<br /> <br /> The second assumption is that you want to be effective monster-hunters. If that's the case, screw just about any Brawl-based fighting style, excepting maybe Kung Fu, and go either Sniper, or that sword one that lets you add automatic damage (obviously I'm assuming here you want to focus on the physical side). Speaking strictly personally, I find this to be intensely dull, not only to play myself, but to see other players doing: not to say they should play according to my opinions, but it's kind of hard to maintain any kind of tension when one human can cut down werewolves like crazy monkeys with a shotgun and/or a katana because they're badasses with 4 Strength, 4 Dex, 5 points in Melee, 5 dots in a broken fighting style and a badass sword. Plus it tends to make you feel kind of useless unless you're as min-maxed as they are. But that's really another topic entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T08:58:20-08:00","id":354777,"title":"","content":"Well I do have legitimate firearm experience &amp; years playing LARP &amp; being one of two people who studied real weapon techniques like Zornhau (we kick so much more butt). So I have a few options I could persue. I just have the most experience with wrestling &amp; don't want to go through the headache of tracking down a sword that could actually be useful in game since I only own display models. Wrestling seemed like a great way to have combat options that were easy to hide. I'm not trying to smuggle guns &amp; swords around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T10:43:20-08:00","id":354882,"title":"","content":"If you're going to be fighting vampires and werewolves, smuggling guns &amp; swords around will quickly become the least of your worries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T18:28:15-08:00","id":355288,"title":"","content":"Well first of all, I'd suggested incorporating weaponry into the wrestling, if not a relic then strangling a werewolf with a silver baton would probably be a lot easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}